WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:01.439
- My name is Michaela Coel.

00:00:01.439 --> 00:00:04.872
I write television and act in television

00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:06.789
and produce television.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.934
The first script I wrote was a play

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.257
and I did that in Drama School

00:00:12.257 --> 00:00:13.713
we were in our final year and they do

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.277
all these really big shows,

00:00:15.277 --> 00:00:17.022
these big kind of period dramas

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:19.246
and I felt like none of those shows

00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:22.160
were representing me as a person

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.646
and I knew that I wouldn't really

00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:25.813
be cast in any of those when I left school

00:00:25.813 --> 00:00:28.396
so I decided to take
myself out of one of those

00:00:28.396 --> 00:00:31.781
plays and write my own
kind of one woman show,

00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:33.438
and that was called Chewing Gum Dreams.

00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:35.020
And so I did that and that was my

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.816
first kind of way into writing.

00:00:37.816 --> 00:00:39.064
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.064 --> 00:00:40.621
I've been quite lucky because I kind of

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:43.690
had a massive big break with my play, but

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.687
it's not very easy.

00:00:45.687 --> 00:00:48.991
Also, people create parts,
and you can't just decide

00:00:48.991 --> 00:00:49.844
you're going to go and get a part,

00:00:49.844 --> 00:00:52.470
you have to audition, you
have to even get in the room.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.032
It's very hard to even get an audition

00:00:54.032 --> 00:00:55.503
so that can be very hard.

00:00:55.503 --> 00:00:57.212
But overall I guess me personally

00:00:57.212 --> 00:01:00.608
the challenges are not getting tired,

00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:04.775
not burning out, I work
very intensely when I write.

00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:08.947
I write for two days
with zero sleep, zero nap

00:01:08.947 --> 00:01:11.828
and that can be very
draining so it's kind of

00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:14.902
about trying to stay healthy with that.

00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:17.521
I never decided I want to be a writer.

00:01:17.521 --> 00:01:21.124
A very kind of unusual
story, for five years

00:01:21.124 --> 00:01:24.364
I was a really devout
christian, and the first day

00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:26.803
I converted to really very
Evangelical, Pentecostal

00:01:26.803 --> 00:01:28.868
Christianity I was given a bible

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.291
and the bible had psalms and proverbs

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.156
and that's when I started writing poetry.

00:01:34.156 --> 00:01:35.856
Then went around performing poetry

00:01:35.856 --> 00:01:37.211
and there was a director in the audience

00:01:37.211 --> 00:01:39.625
and he said you should try acting.

00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:42.304
So I did, and that was in 2009.

00:01:42.304 --> 00:01:45.137
So it's all just kind of happened.

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:49.357
Where do I find time to write

00:01:50.215 --> 00:01:51.636
and then be in other people's shows?

00:01:51.636 --> 00:01:55.432
I guess I've been quite
lucky with my schedule.

00:01:55.432 --> 00:01:58.661
So next year I won't really
do much writing at all,

00:01:58.661 --> 00:02:00.600
it's just going to be
acting the whole year.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.175
This year has been very heavy on writing

00:02:03.175 --> 00:02:04.282
and acting really.

00:02:04.282 --> 00:02:05.428
You just make it work.

00:02:05.428 --> 00:02:09.595
I think if you really want
to do it you make it work.

